.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NQPWENC 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqpwenc ,
.Nm nqpwdec
.Nd keep a secret key under a passphrase
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqpwenc
.Fa "const uint8_t *pw" "size_t pwlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ad" "size_t alen"
.Fa "uint32_t m" "uint32_t t" "uint32_t p"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqpwdec
.Fa "const uint8_t *pw" "size_t pwlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ad" "size_t alen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *sk" "size_t cap" "size_t *sklen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqpwenc
encrypts the secret key
.Fa sk
(1 to
.Dv NQPWMAX ,
65536, bytes) under the passphrase
.Fa pw
(1 to
.Dv NQPWLEN ,
4096, bytes) in the format noqtis-pwkey-1, and
.Fn nqpwdec
decrypts it.
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1
writes such keys, and
.Xr noqtis-sign 1
and
.Xr noqtis-dec 1
read them, with the key file's first line as
.Fa ad .
.Pp
The format, all numbers big-endian:
.Bl -column "ciphertext of sk" "sklen" -offset indent
.It Sy field Ta Sy bytes
.It Li NQPW Ta 4
.It version, 1 Ta 1
.It KDF, 1: Argon2id 0x13 Ta 1
.It AEAD, 1: ChaCha20-Poly1305 Ta 1
.It Fa m , No KiB Ta 4
.It Fa t , No passes Ta 4
.It Fa p , No lanes Ta 4
.It salt, random Ta 16
.It ciphertext of Fa sk Ta Fa sklen
.It tag Ta 16
.El
.Pp
Argon2id
.Pq Xr nqa2id 3
of the passphrase and the salt with
.Fa t ,
.Fa m
and
.Fa p
gives 44 bytes: the AEAD's key and its nonce.
The associated data is the 35-byte header followed by
.Fa ad
(at most 1024 bytes;
.Dv NULL
with 0 for none), so no field of the header and no byte of
.Fa ad
can change without the tag failing.
The output is
.Fa sklen
+
.Dv NQPWOVH
(51) bytes.
.Pp
.Fa m ,
.Fa t
and
.Fa p
are 0 for the defaults
.Dv NQPWM
(65536 KiB, 64 MiB),
.Dv NQPWT
(3) and
.Dv NQPWP
(4).
Both functions enforce the same limits: memory
.Dv NQPWMMIN
(8 MiB) to
.Dv NQPWMMAX
(1 GiB), 1 to
.Dv NQPWTMAX
(16) passes, 1 to
.Dv NQPWPMAX
(16) lanes, and
.Fa m
\(mu
.Fa t
at most
.Dv NQPWWORK
(4194304, 4 GiB of passes).
.Fn nqpwdec
checks the magic, version, algorithms, parameters and size before it
derives anything, so a file cannot make it take more than 1 GiB or more
than 4 GiB of passes; then a wrong passphrase, a changed byte or
another
.Fa ad
fails the tag.
On any error
.Fa sk
is zeroed, and
.Fn nqpwenc
leaves nothing in
.Fa out .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ,
or
.Bl -tag -width NQEMEM
.It Bq Er NQEARG
A passphrase that is empty or too long, an
.Fa ad
over 1024 bytes, a key that is empty or too long, parameters outside
the limits (for
.Fn nqpwenc ) ,
or a
.Dv NULL
pointer.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa cap
is too small;
.Pf * Fa outlen
or
.Pf * Fa sklen
gets the size needed.
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
.Fa in
is not noqtis-pwkey-1 (magic, version, KDF or AEAD), or is too short.
.It Bq Er NQELIM
.Fa in
asks for parameters outside the limits, or holds a key over
.Dv NQPWMAX .
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
The passphrase is wrong, or a byte of
.Fa in
or
.Fa ad
differs.
.It Bq Er NQEMEM
Argon2id's memory could not be allocated.
.It Bq Er NQERNG
The salt could not be drawn.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqa2id 3
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 9106 (Argon2id), RFC 8439 (ChaCha20-Poly1305).
